Hang location-bar bubbles below the shell's top bar.

The save password bubble, and every other LocationBarBubbleDelegateView,
points at a button in Chromium's toolbar or location bar. This port draws its
browser UI in ArkTS: that toolbar is hidden at the top of the window, under
the status bar and the address bar the shell draws over the page, so these
bubbles opened with their title -- and on the save password bubble its
picture -- behind them. On OHOS they now hang from the line just below the
shell's top bar, centred, the way the page-info bubbles already do
(GetPageInfoAnchorRect, ohos-phone-dialogs.patch).

Generated against Chromium 154.0.8037.51 with chromium-154-harmonyos.patch
applied. Apply with:
  git apply ohos-location-bar-bubble-below-shell.patch

